body.statement:
There exist universal constants \(0<c<C<\infty\) such that, uniformly along every sequence satisfying \(d\to\infty\) and \(d=o(\sqrt n)\),
\[
\Pr_{G_n}\!\left\{
c\frac{(d+1)^2}{n\log(d+2)}
\le R_2(G)\le C\frac{d^2}{n}
\right\}\longrightarrow1.
\]
Equivalently, the lower endpoint is \(c r(n,d)\).  This is a logarithmic-width two-sided bracket; it does not identify an exact frontier and does not assert that the capsule attains its lower endpoint.
